## 🎯 Quick Reference

**From Documentation:**

All examples come from the official docs. Fence labels have been corrected.

### 1. Scaffold and run locally (Quick Start)

```bash
npx @inkeep/create-agents my-agents
cd my-agents
pnpm setup-dev   # Docker must be running
pnpm dev         # Visual Builder auto-opens at http://localhost:3000
```

Log in with `INKEEP_AGENTS_MANAGE_UI_USERNAME` and `INKEEP_AGENTS_MANAGE_UI_PASSWORD` from the root `.env`.

### 2. Define an agent with a router and specialists (TypeScript SDK)

```typescript
import { agent, subAgent } from '@inkeep/agents-sdk';

const routerSubAgent = subAgent({
  id: 'support-router',
  name: 'Support Router',
  prompt: 'Route customer inquiries to appropriate specialists',
  canTransferTo: () => [billingSubAgent],
});

const billingSubAgent = subAgent({
  id: 'billing-specialist',
  name: 'Billing Specialist',
  prompt: 'Handle billing and payment inquiries',
});

export const customerSupportAgent = agent({
  defaultSubAgent: routerSubAgent,
  subAgents: () => [routerSubAgent, billingSubAgent],
});
```

### 3. Transfer vs. delegate (TypeScript SDK)

```typescript
// TRANSFER: user will likely have follow-up questions about their order
const routerSubAgent = subAgent({
  id: 'router',
  prompt: 'For order inquiries, transfer to order specialist',
  canTransferTo: () => [orderSubAgent],
});

// DELEGATION: just need a quick calculation, then continue
const mathSupervisor = subAgent({
  id: 'supervisor',
  prompt: 'Delegate to number producers, then add results together',
  canDelegateTo: () => [numberProducerA, numberProducerB],
});
```

External A2A agents are delegated to the same way: `canDelegateTo: () => [myExternalAgent]`.

### 4. Register an MCP server as a tool

```typescript
import { subAgent, mcpTool } from '@inkeep/agents-sdk';

const knowledgeBaseTool = mcpTool({
  id: 'knowledge-base-tool',
  name: 'knowledge_base',
  description: 'Search the company knowledge base for information',
  serverUrl: 'https://kb.yourcompany.com/mcp',
});

const qaAgent = subAgent({
  id: 'qa-agent',
  name: 'QA Agent',
  description: 'Answers questions about the company knowledge base.',
  prompt: 'You answer questions using the knowledge base tool.',
  canUse: () => [knowledgeBaseTool],
});
```

To narrow the tool surface, use `canUse: () => [zendeskMcpTool.with({ selectedTools: ['create_zendesk_ticket'] })]`. To rename or reword a tool for the model, use `toolOverrides`.

### 5. Environment-aware credentials

```typescript
import { mcpTool } from '@inkeep/agents-sdk';
import { envSettings } from '../environments';

export const stripeTool = mcpTool({
  id: 'stripe-tool',
  name: 'Stripe',
  serverUrl: 'https://mcp.stripe.com/mcp',
  credential: envSettings.getEnvironmentCredential('stripe_api_key'),
});
```

```bash
export INKEEP_ENV=production
inkeep push                    # uses production
inkeep push --env development  # flag overrides env var
```

### 6. Model configuration and inheritance

```typescript
// Project level (required): base model
models: {
  base: {
    model: 'anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5',
    providerOptions: { temperature: 0.7, maxOutputTokens: 2048 },
  },
},

// Override per agent / sub agent
const myAgent = agent({ models: { base: { model: 'openai/gpt-5.2' } } });
const mySubAgent = subAgent({
  models: { structuredOutput: { model: 'openai/gpt-4.1-mini' } },
});
```

Model slots are `base`, `structuredOutput` and `summarizer`. Each one inherits independently down project → agent → sub agent. A pinned model (`anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-20250514`) never changes. An unpinned model (`anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5`) follows the provider's latest version. When `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY` is set, `fallbackModels` and `allowedProviders` become available.

### 7. Headers → context fetcher → prompt variables

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';
import { subAgent } from '@inkeep/agents-sdk';
import { contextConfig, fetchDefinition, headers } from '@inkeep/agents-core';

const h = headers({
  schema: z.object({ user_id: z.string(), auth_token: z.string() }),
});

const userFetcher = fetchDefinition({
  id: 'user-info',
  name: 'User Information',
  trigger: 'initialization',
  fetchConfig: {
    url: `https://api.example.com/users/${h.toTemplate('user_id')}`,
    method: 'GET',
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${h.toTemplate('auth_token')}` },
    transform: 'user',
  },
  responseSchema: z.object({ user: z.object({ name: z.string() }) }),
  defaultValue: 'Guest User',
});

const ctx = contextConfig({ headers: h, contextVariables: { user: userFetcher } });

const assistant = subAgent({
  id: 'personal-assistant',
  name: 'Personal Assistant',
  prompt: `You help ${ctx.toTemplate('user.name')}.`,
});
```

Use **lowercase** header keys. In Visual Builder JSON, the same headers can be templated as `"Authorization": "Bearer {{headers.auth-token}}"`.

### 8. Call an agent from your app (Vercel AI SDK provider)

```typescript
import { streamText } from 'ai';
import { createInkeep } from '@inkeep/ai-sdk-provider';

const inkeep = createInkeep({
  baseURL: process.env.INKEEP_AGENTS_API_URL,
  apiKey: '<your-agent-api-key>', // agent ID is encoded in the key
  headers: { 'x-emit-operations': 'true' }, // stream tool events
});

const result = await streamText({ model: inkeep(), prompt: 'Plan an event in NYC' });
```

Install it with `npm install @inkeep/ai-sdk-provider ai`.

### 9. Raw chat call with headers (curl)

```bash
curl -N -X POST "http://localhost:3003/api/chat" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $INKEEP_API_KEY" \
  -H "user_id: u_123" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"What can you help me with?"}],"conversationId":"conv-123"}'
```

### 10. Webhook trigger

```typescript
import { agent, trigger, subAgent } from '@inkeep/agents-sdk';

const slackTrigger = trigger({
  name: 'Slack Messages',
  description: 'Handle incoming Slack messages',
  messageTemplate: 'New message from {{user.name}}: {{text}}',
});

export default agent({
  id: 'support-agent',
  name: 'Support Agent',
  defaultSubAgent: subAgent({ id: 'support', name: 'Support Assistant', prompt: 'You help answer support questions.' }),
  triggers: () => [slackTrigger],
});
```

### 11. Structured output with a data component

```typescript
import { dataComponent } from '@inkeep/agents-sdk';
import { z } from 'zod';

export const taskList = dataComponent({
  id: 'task-list',
  name: 'TaskList',
  description: 'Display user tasks with status',
  props: z.object({
    tasks: z.array(z.object({
      id: z.string().describe('Unique task identifier'),
      title: z.string().describe('Task title'),
      completed: z.boolean().describe('Whether the task is completed'),
    })).describe('Array of user tasks'),
  }),
});
```

### 12. CLI config and push/pull

```typescript
// inkeep.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from '@inkeep/agents-cli/config';
import 'dotenv/config';

export default defineConfig({
  tenantId: 'my-company',
  agentsApi: { url: 'http://localhost:3002', apiKey: process.env.API_KEY },
  outputDirectory: './output',
});
```

```bash
inkeep push                                   # code → Visual Builder (whole project)
inkeep pull                                   # Visual Builder → code
inkeep push --agents-api-url https://api.production.com
```

### 13. Skills attached to a Sub Agent

```typescript
import path from 'node:path';
import { loadSkills, project, subAgent } from '@inkeep/agents-sdk';

const activitiesPlanner = subAgent({
  id: 'activities-planner',
  name: 'Activities Planner',
  prompt: 'Help users plan activities based on current weather.',
  skills: () => [{ id: 'weather-safety-guardrails', index: 0 }],
});

export const myProject = project({
  id: 'my-project',
  name: 'My Project',
  agents: () => [myAgent],
  skills: () => loadSkills(path.join('my-project/skills')),
  models: { base: { model: 'openai/gpt-4o' } },
});
```

Skills live in `skills/<skill-id>/SKILL.md`, with optional `reference/` and `templates/` folders.

### 14. Function tool (Visual Builder)

```javascript
function calculateBMI({ weight, height }) {
  const bmi = weight / (height * height);
  let category = 'Normal';
  if (bmi < 18.5) category = 'Underweight';
  else if (bmi >= 30) category = 'Obese';
  return { bmi: Math.round(bmi * 10) / 10, category };
}
```

You can pin npm dependencies with a version map such as `{ "axios": "1.6.0", "lodash": "4.17.21" }`.

### 15. Self-host the external services (Docker, any Linux VM)

```bash
git clone https://github.com/inkeep/agents-optional-local-dev inkeep-external-services
cd inkeep-external-services
./scripts/generate-env-from-example.sh   # creates .env from .env.docker.example
```

This brings up SigNoz, Nango, the OTEL Collector and Jaeger, and can take about 5 minutes. Set `NANGO_ENCRYPTION_KEY` once; it **cannot be changed later**. For a custom image, run `docker compose build && docker compose up -d`.

### 16. Prompt skeleton (Agent Engineering guide)

```text
You are [role identity] who [what excellence looks like in practice].

You [concrete positive behavior].
You [concrete positive behavior].
You [concrete positive behavior].
```

For orchestrator prompts, the tutorials use `<workflow>` and `<rules>` blocks, for example "Always delegate in order: Meeting Finder → Company Research".

